CAT = "dkMotorway"; SEG = "MWY"
Q = [
("Which vehicles may use a Danish motorway?",
 "Those that can do 50 km/h", ["Any road vehicle at all", "Cars, mopeds and bicycles", "Only private cars and lorries"],
 "Motorways and their slip roads are only for motor vehicles that may lawfully drive at least 50 km/h."),
("On the stretches where it is allowed, what is the top speed on a Danish motorway?",
 "130 km/h", ["110 km/h", "120 km/h", "140 km/h"],
 "The highest permitted speed on motorways and their slip roads is 130 km/h. Many stretches are signed lower, so watch the signs."),
("You tow a trailer without tempo 100 approval on a motorway. What is your limit?",
 "80 km/h", ["70 km/h", "100 km/h", "110 km/h"],
 "A car with a trailer may do at most 80 km/h on a motorway, or 100 km/h if the combination is approved for tempo 100."),
("You join a motorway where the slip road merges. How do you signal?",
 "Left indicator", ["Right indicator", "Hazard lights", "No signal"],
 "Signal left when joining, match your speed to the traffic in the nearest lane and merge into a suitable gap."),
("Shark's teeth and a give-way sign stand at the end of a short slip road. What does it mean?",
 "Give way to motorway traffic", ["Motorway traffic gives way", "Stop on the hard shoulder first", "Merge without looking back"],
 "Normally you merge, but where a give-way line and sign are shown, you exceptionally have an unconditional duty to give way when joining."),
("You have merged onto the E45 and the road is clear. Where do you settle?",
 "The right-hand lane", ["The left-hand lane", "The middle lane", "Any lane you like best"],
 "Keep to the middle of the right-hand lane and use the lane to its left only to overtake, to make room for joining traffic or to follow signed lanes."),
("Which of these is lawful on a Danish motorway?",
 "Stop at an emergency phone", ["A U-turn at a gap", "Reversing back to an exit", "Parking on the hard shoulder"],
 "U-turns, reversing, crossing the central reserve, stopping and parking are banned on motorways and slip roads. You may stop at an emergency phone only to call for help."),
("You must repair your car on the motorway using part of a lane. What must you do first?",
 "Phone the police on 114", ["Nothing, just be quick", "Switch on the fog lights", "Phone a friend for help"],
 "Repairs on a motorway are only allowed if needed to move the car. If part of the carriageway must be used, contact the police on 114 first; not needed if the whole car is on the hard shoulder."),
("Traffic ahead on the motorway suddenly stops in an unexpected queue. What must you do?",
 "Use your hazard lights", ["Flash your main beam", "Sound the horn twice", "Switch on your rear fog light"],
 "On motorways you must use your hazard lights to warn traffic behind of an unexpected queue or other immediate danger."),
("You want to move two lanes to the left on a motorway. How should you do it?",
 "One lane at a time", ["Both lanes in one move", "Without signalling", "Only from a standstill"],
 "Change only one lane at a time, signalling and checking mirrors and blind spots before each move."),
("You are approaching your exit. When should you move into the right-hand lane?",
 "Well before the slip road", ["At the start of the slip road", "Only once you see the exit", "After braking on the motorway"],
 "Move into the right lane in good time before the exit, signal right early, and avoid slowing down on the motorway itself."),
("On a combined entry and exit lane, a car ahead is joining just where you want to leave. What should you do?",
 "Let it in first", ["Speed up to block it", "Leave before it at once", "Brake hard to stop"],
 "On a combined slip lane, give room for the vehicle ahead to join before you leave."),
("You drive a car and caravan longer than 7 m on a motorway with three lanes each way. Which lanes may you use?",
 "The two right-hand lanes", ["Only the left-hand lane", "Any of the three lanes", "Only the middle lane"],
 "On motorways with three or more lanes in your direction, combinations over 7 m may only use the two lanes furthest right."),
("Your car dies on the E20 and you get it onto the hard shoulder. Where should everyone wait for help?",
 "Behind the crash barrier", ["In the car with belts on", "At the edge of the hard shoulder", "On the verge beside the car"],
 "Leave the car carefully, put on reflective vests and wait off the carriageway, ideally behind the crash barrier."),
("A friend offers to tow your broken-down car off the motorway with a rope. Is that allowed?",
 "No, towing is banned", ["Yes, below 30 km/h", "Yes, with hazard lights", "Yes, on the hard shoulder"],
 "Towing on a motorway is forbidden, except by an approved recovery vehicle."),
("You drive on a motortrafikvej (expressway). What is the general speed limit?",
 "80 km/h", ["60 km/h", "100 km/h", "130 km/h"],
 "On an expressway (motortrafikvej) the limit is 80 km/h, but signs can raise it locally to up to 100 km/h."),
("What extra danger does an expressway (motortrafikvej) have compared with a motorway?",
 "Oncoming traffic, no barrier", ["Cyclists in every lane", "A higher speed limit", "No slip roads anywhere on it"],
 "Expressways seldom have a central reserve, so oncoming traffic can cross the centre, and both drivers and pedestrians may cross at junctions."),
("At the 1,500 m exit sign, what does it show besides the distance?",
 "The exit's number and name", ["Current fuel prices", "The speed limit ahead", "The weather further ahead"],
 "The 1,500 m exit sign gives the exit number and name, and usually the next exit and its distance."),
("A lane is marked BUS and separated by a solid edge line. Who may use it?",
 "Only buses in service", ["All cars at rush hour", "Any vehicle if empty", "Lorries and vans"],
 "The word BUS in a lane bounded by a solid edge line or double solid line means only buses in service may use it, unless other symbols allow others."),
("A lane has a cycle symbol and a solid edge line. What is it?",
 "A cycle track", ["A parking lane", "A bus lane", "An overtaking lane"],
 "A cycle symbol in a lane bounded by a solid edge line marks it as a cycle track for cyclists and small mopeds."),
('A continuous yellow line is painted along the kerb of a Copenhagen street. Which of these is allowed there?',
 'Only stops forced by traffic', ['Parking for up to one hour', 'Loading goods briefly', 'Dropping off a passenger quickly'],
 'A solid yellow kerb line means stopping is forbidden, except when traffic forces you to stop. A dashed yellow line means parking is forbidden.'),
("You stop for 2 minutes beside a broken yellow kerb line to drop off a friend. Is that allowed in Denmark?",
 "Yes, a short stop is allowed", ["No, all stopping is banned", "Only with hazard lights on", "Only for taxis and buses"],
 "A dashed yellow line on the kerb or road edge means no parking, so a stop under 3 minutes or to let people in or out is allowed. A solid yellow line bans stopping altogether."),
("Beside the road stands a round sign: blue inside, red border, a single red slash. What does it mean?",
 "No parking", ["No stopping", "No entry", "End of limits"],
 "One red diagonal line means no parking on that side of the road; a red cross means no stopping."),
("You drop a friend outside a shop in Horsens. The free kerb space nearest the zebra crossing ends 3 m before it. May you stop there?",
 "No, keep at least 5 m away", ["Yes, for under 3 minutes", "Yes, with hazard lights on", "Yes, if no one is crossing"],
 "Stopping and parking are forbidden on a pedestrian crossing or within 5 m before it, even for a quick drop-off."),
("In a town street there are no parking bays near the crossroads. How close to the crossing road may you stop?",
 "No closer than 10 m", ["No closer than 5 m", "No closer than 15 m", "No closer than 30 m"],
 "Stopping and parking are forbidden in a junction or within 10 m of the nearest edge of the crossing carriageway or cycle track, except in marked bays."),
("You want to park near a level crossing in the countryside. What distance must you keep from it?",
 "No closer than 30 m", ["No closer than 5 m", "No closer than 10 m", "No closer than 50 m"],
 "Parking is forbidden within 30 m of a level crossing, and stopping is forbidden on the crossing itself."),
("Where there is no yellow kerb marking, how far either side of a bus stop sign is stopping banned?",
 "12 m", ["5 m", "10 m", "20 m"],
 "Stopping and parking are forbidden at a bus stop and within 12 m on either side of the sign. Yellow kerb marking can extend the ban."),
("You stop for 2 minutes at the kerb to let a passenger out. Is this parking?",
 "No", ["Yes", "Only at night", "Only in towns"],
 "Stopping for under 3 minutes, or to let people in or out, or to load or unload, is not parking."),
("On an ordinary two-way road, may you park on the left-hand side?",
 "Quiet or one-way roads only", ["Yes, anywhere at any time", "Only at night after 22:00", "Only when loading heavy goods"],
 "Stopping and parking on the left side of the road is forbidden, except on less busy roads and one-way roads."),
("You want a short break on a main road (hovedvej) between two towns. May you park on the carriageway?",
 "No, not on the carriageway", ["Yes, anywhere at all", "Yes, with hazard lights on", "Only for up to an hour"],
 "Parking on the carriageway of a main road outside built-up areas is forbidden. Use a lay-by or car park."),
("A time plate under a parking sign shows times in brackets. When do they apply?",
 "Saturday", ["Sunday", "Weekdays", "Holidays"],
 "Black or white times apply on weekdays except Saturday, times in brackets on Saturdays, and red times on Sundays and public holidays."),
("You park at the kerb in a built-up area at night with a normal car. Which lights are enough?",
 "Parking and rear light", ["Main beam on the road side", "Hazard lights all night", "No lights at all"],
 "In built-up areas you need only the parking light and rear light on the side facing the middle of the road."),
("Your passenger wants to take a photo, and you consider pulling over briefly. Where is even a short stop forbidden?",
 "On a bridge over a motorway", ["In a lay-by", "In a marked parking bay", "On a quiet residential street"],
 "Stopping and parking are forbidden on a bridge over a motorway, in an underpass or in a tunnel, and near a hill crest or blind bend."),
("At night, which lights are not enough on their own while driving?",
 "Daytime running lights", ["Dipped beam alone", "Main beam alone", "Dipped beam plus front fog lights"],
 "Daytime running lights do not meet the lighting rules for the lighting-up time. Use at least dipped beam."),
("At night you see reflector posts beside the road. What colour reflector marks the right-hand side?",
 "Orange", ["White", "Yellow", "Green"],
 "Edge posts have orange reflectors on the right side of the road and white reflectors on the left."),
("Headlights coming towards you on a dark road are blinding you. Where do you direct your eyes?",
 "Along the right edge", ["Straight into the lights", "At the centre line", "Down at your speedometer"],
 "Avoid looking into the lights. Look ahead along the right edge of the road for obstacles, and slow down if you cannot see."),
("You meet a car on a narrow, completely dark road. What is a suitable highest speed?",
 "40 km/h", ["20 km/h", "60 km/h", "80 km/h"],
 "When meeting on narrow, fully dark roads, slow to at most 40 km/h so you can stop for anything hidden beyond your dipped beam."),
("In a tunnel, a red X lights up over your lane. What must you do?",
 "Leave the lane at once", ["Slow down to 50 km/h", "Stop in the lane and wait", "Stay in the lane and go on"],
 "A red X means the lane must be left immediately. A yellow flashing arrow means move soon to the lane shown; a green arrow means the lane is open."),
("In a tunnel, a red X shows over every lane. What does that mean?",
 "Do not drive on", ["Use any lane", "Speed up to leave", "Drive on with care"],
 "A red X over all lanes means no further driving: stop and follow instructions."),
("A yellow arrow flashes over your lane in a tunnel. What should you do?",
 "Move to the lane shown", ["Stop where you are now", "Turn on your hazard lights", "Reverse out of the tunnel"],
 "A flashing yellow arrow means change to the lane it points to as soon as you safely can."),
("A fire breaks out in a tunnel. How should you call for help if you can?",
 "The emergency phone", ["A text from your mobile", "A long blast of the horn", "Flashing your headlights"],
 "Use the tunnel's emergency phone rather than a mobile when calling for help. In many tunnels, opening the alarm cabinet automatically puts a red X over the right-hand lane."),
("A red light flashes before a stop line (rødt blinksignal). What must you do?",
 "Stop before the line", ["Go on with extra care", "Slow down to 30 km/h", "Sound your horn and go"],
 "A flashing red signal means stop before the stop line or at a safe distance before the signal, for example at a level crossing or tunnel."),
("Why must you take extra care near light rail (letbane) trains?",
 "They take long to stop", ["They must always give way to cars", "They only run late at night", "They stop at every junction"],
 "Light rail trains are heavy and need a long braking distance, so they cannot stop quickly for a car on the track."),
("A give-way sign has a plate saying 'Letbane'. What does it mean?",
 "A light rail line crosses", ["A bus lane ends here", "A railway station is near", "Cyclists cross the road here"],
 "The plate shows that the crossing road has a light rail line with trains in both directions. Give way and watch both ways."),
("A signal shows a white bar instead of coloured lights. Who does it apply to?",
 "Buses, light rail, some cars", ["All cars and vans", "Pedestrians only", "Cyclists and small moped riders"],
 "The white bus and light rail signal applies to buses in service, light rail vehicles and zero-emission cars. Other drivers follow the ordinary signals."),
("You drive in dense traffic beside a lorry. What is the main danger?",
 "Its blind spots", ["Its loud engine noise", "Its bright headlights", "Its lower speed limit"],
 "Lorries and buses have large blind spots, and their driver may not see you when changing lanes or turning. Do not stay beside them longer than needed."),
("You park on a slope in Vejle and pop into a bakery for five minutes. Which step does the law expect?",
 "Lock it and take the key", ["Leave the key in the ignition", "Leave the engine running", "Leave it in neutral on the slope"],
 "Before leaving the car, make sure it cannot start moving by itself and cannot be used by others: parking brake on and the car locked with the key taken."),
("You are parked on a street with a cycle lane beside you and want to get out. What do you check first?",
 "No cyclist or car is coming", ["The pavement is empty", "The engine is switched off", "The handbrake warning light is on"],
 "Opening a door must not cause danger or undue inconvenience. Look behind for cyclists and cars before you open it."),
]
